WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.040 --> 00:00:06.480
The arrival of Stinger, Kang's new fashion
sense, and a familiar looking cantina.

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:12.230
The "Ant-Man and the Wasp: Quantumania" trailer
was filled with Easter eggs you might have

00:00:12.230 --> 00:00:13.230
missed.

00:00:13.230 --> 00:00:16.619
Forget about saving the universe, Scott Lang's
greatest accomplishments are the victories

00:00:16.619 --> 00:00:18.880
he encounters in his everyday life.

00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:23.060
For example, in "Ant-Man and the Wasp," his
daughter gives him a "World's Greatest Grandma"

00:00:23.060 --> 00:00:27.740
trophy, which, at the time, was the best birthday
present Scott ever received.

00:00:27.740 --> 00:00:32.630
However, that accolade pales in comparison
to being hailed as one of the best workers

00:00:32.630 --> 00:00:34.750
ever to grace the ice cream industry.

00:00:34.750 --> 00:00:39.790
The "Ant-Man and the Wasp: Quantumania" trailer
notes that Scott is Baskin-Robbins' "Employee

00:00:39.790 --> 00:00:41.000
of the Century."

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:46.150
And that's in addition to being an ex-con,
successful podcaster, and member of the Avengers.

00:00:46.150 --> 00:00:51.190
He even stops by in his Ant-Man suit to accept
the award, showing just how far he's come

00:00:51.190 --> 00:00:53.660
since his days of being down on his luck.

00:00:53.660 --> 00:00:57.710
It's great to see that superheroism hasn't
made Scott forget about his days working in

00:00:57.710 --> 00:00:58.940
an ice cream parlor.

00:00:58.940 --> 00:01:03.690
Furthermore, the trailer also reveals that
Dale will be part of "Ant-Man and the Wasp:

00:01:03.690 --> 00:01:07.050
Quantumania," as one scene shows Scott shaking
hands with his old manager.

00:01:07.050 --> 00:01:12.939
The "Ant-Man and the Wasp: Quantumania" trailer
doesn't explain specifically how the Ant-Man

00:01:12.939 --> 00:01:15.220
family gets sucked into the Quantum Realm.

00:01:15.220 --> 00:01:19.620
We can only assume that it's because the film's
primary villain, Kang the Conqueror, somehow

00:01:19.620 --> 00:01:22.869
uses Cassie's new tech for his own schemes.

00:01:22.869 --> 00:01:27.370
Throughout the trailer, Janet seems terrified
of anything relating to the Quantum Realm,

00:01:27.370 --> 00:01:31.649
saying that there's some information she didn't
share with everyone else.

00:01:31.649 --> 00:01:33.869
"There's something I never told you…"

00:01:33.869 --> 00:01:38.200
The trailer makes it seem like she's talking
about Kang, who looks to be in control down

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:42.060
there, or at least has a very imposing presence.

00:01:42.060 --> 00:01:45.079
Could Kang be the reason why everyone's in
the Quantum Realm?

00:01:45.079 --> 00:01:48.130
Is he chasing after Janet for something she
did there?

00:01:48.130 --> 00:01:50.880
Did Cassie's technology somehow "awaken" him?

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:55.719
MCU fans will remember that "Ant-Man and the
Wasp" revealed that Janet spent 30 years in

00:01:55.719 --> 00:01:58.100
the Quantum Realm before Scott rescued her.

00:01:58.100 --> 00:02:01.799
There's no telling what kind of trouble she
got into during that time, but "Ant-Man and

00:02:01.799 --> 00:02:06.280
the Wasp: Quantumania" will definitely give
us some answers.

00:02:06.280 --> 00:02:10.729
The clue was in the title as to where Scott
and Hope would spend their next adventure,

00:02:10.729 --> 00:02:15.870
but now the new trailer confirms that they're
not the only ones headed to the Quantum Realm.

00:02:15.870 --> 00:02:20.531
After Cassie's quantum satellite apparently
makes contact with all the wrong people, all

00:02:20.531 --> 00:02:24.620
of Ant-Man's allies are pulled along with
him into a strange new world.

00:02:24.620 --> 00:02:27.410
"It's a secret universe beneath ours."

00:02:27.410 --> 00:02:33.239
From here, the trailer lays on the stunning
and surreal vistas of the Quantum Realm pretty

00:02:33.239 --> 00:02:34.239
thick.

00:02:34.239 --> 00:02:37.740
This latest installment of Ant-man's story
feels less like it's pulled off of a comic

00:02:37.740 --> 00:02:43.400
book page, but instead from a classic science
fiction movie involving another small adventure.

00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:49.870
This could very well be Scott Lang's own "Fantastic
Voyage," the classic 1966 film with a group

00:02:49.870 --> 00:02:54.790
of explorers shrunk to microscopic size who
traverse the insides of a living human body.

00:02:54.790 --> 00:02:58.970
While there doesn't seem to be any human test
subject in the area when they're shrunk down,

00:02:58.970 --> 00:03:02.849
"Quantumania" seems to match the epic adventure
on a tiny scale.

00:03:02.849 --> 00:03:07.010
One shot suggests that when they arrive, the
group ends up scattered across this unknown

00:03:07.010 --> 00:03:08.010
territory.

00:03:08.010 --> 00:03:11.870
This could lead to some father-daughter time
with Scott and Cassie, and Hope getting the

00:03:11.870 --> 00:03:16.070
opportunity to know the mother she thought
she lost forever.

00:03:16.070 --> 00:03:20.099
It's hard to ignore the fact that a bar seen
during our peek into the Quantum Realm as

00:03:20.099 --> 00:03:24.670
the trailer plays out feels like a visual
callback to the "Star Wars" saga.

00:03:24.670 --> 00:03:30.010
The circular half-bar, its multi-armed bartender,
and the well-packed room definitely harken

00:03:30.010 --> 00:03:31.810
back to the Mos Eisley Cantina.

00:03:31.810 --> 00:03:36.040
The bar in the trailer seems to have more
of an air of sophistication that Mos Eisley

00:03:36.040 --> 00:03:37.040
lacks.

00:03:37.040 --> 00:03:41.459
But several patrons are seen wearing brown
cloaks reminiscent of Obi-Wan Kenobi and his

00:03:41.459 --> 00:03:43.090
protegé Luke Skywalker.

00:03:43.090 --> 00:03:47.310
The earth-toned outfits feel like a callback
to the Empire, and many of the characters

00:03:47.310 --> 00:03:51.950
seen within the establishment resemble the
rubber-faced puppets of the sci-fi classic.

00:03:51.950 --> 00:03:56.700
In "Ant-Man and The Wasp: Quantumania," however,
there's a lot more neon involved, and the

00:03:56.700 --> 00:03:59.250
lighting is generally warmer in tone.

00:03:59.250 --> 00:04:04.060
There are also what appear to be strange hookahs
sitting on several of the tables.

00:04:04.060 --> 00:04:09.900
Fans will have to wait to see how these devices,
and the bar itself, will be used in the film.

00:04:09.900 --> 00:04:14.110
Cassie is one of the most significant reveals
in the "Ant-Man and the Wasp: Quantumania"

00:04:14.110 --> 00:04:15.110
trailer.

00:04:15.110 --> 00:04:18.340
She shows her dad the device she helped make,
which communicates with the Quantum Realm.

00:04:18.340 --> 00:04:22.270
After the group is sucked into the realm,
we see Cassie in her regular street clothes

00:04:22.270 --> 00:04:23.270
with her dad.

00:04:23.270 --> 00:04:28.680
Eventually, toward the end of the trailer,
we see Scott, Hope, and Cassie all in special

00:04:28.680 --> 00:04:31.630
suits as they stare down someone off-screen.

00:04:31.630 --> 00:04:35.810
While we've seen Scott and Hope's suits before,
Cassie's is new.

00:04:35.810 --> 00:04:39.930
It looks like we might see Cassie take on
the mantle of "Stature" in the third "Ant-Man"

00:04:39.930 --> 00:04:40.930
flick.

00:04:40.930 --> 00:04:45.520
We first saw poster art of Cassie's purple
suit at San Diego Comic-Con 2022, and now

00:04:45.520 --> 00:04:47.160
it's finally a reality.

00:04:47.160 --> 00:04:51.860
In the comics, Stature makes her debut in
2006's "Young Avengers" #2 and later becomes

00:04:51.860 --> 00:04:55.669
Stinger in 2016's "Astonishing Ant-Man" #6.

00:04:55.669 --> 00:04:59.610
Cassie's powers are very much like that of
Scotts, but they can often be connected to

00:04:59.610 --> 00:05:00.610
her emotions.

00:05:00.610 --> 00:05:05.650
It seems like "Ant-Man and the Wasp: Quantumania"
will introduce us to a new MCU hero who could

00:05:05.650 --> 00:05:08.509
appear in future films.

00:05:08.509 --> 00:05:14.040
All it took was a scene-stealing monologue
in "Loki" and blurry camera footage from D23

00:05:14.040 --> 00:05:18.639
to get fans hyped about Jonathan Majors' next
take on Kang.

00:05:18.639 --> 00:05:23.840
An outstanding performance was always guaranteed,
but the fact that this appearance would potentially

00:05:23.840 --> 00:05:28.789
be completely different from what we had before
was even more exciting.

00:05:28.789 --> 00:05:34.449
It only takes a few seconds to confirm that
this Kang isn't quite as jovial as the one

00:05:34.449 --> 00:05:38.110
before, and he might have some plans for…conquest.

00:05:38.110 --> 00:05:44.850
"So, what's it gonna be…Ant-Man?"

00:05:44.850 --> 00:05:48.630
In the trailer, we first get a good look at
him in his iconic get-up from the comics,

00:05:48.630 --> 00:05:51.220
which originates from the 40th century.

00:05:51.220 --> 00:05:55.750
From there, the Conquerer-to-be is shown having
a brief chat with Scott, with Kang coming

00:05:55.750 --> 00:06:00.370
off as far more threatening than the jokey
anarchist we met before.

00:06:00.370 --> 00:06:06.240
Our only questions are how Scott will hold
off against this new and unknown threat, and

00:06:06.240 --> 00:06:10.780
will the joint help of Cassie and Hope be
enough to ensure that the Kang Dynasty is

00:06:10.780 --> 00:06:13.099
held off for as long as possible?

